<title>PAKISTAN: Pakistan cotton rates hold steady.</title>
<headline>Pakistan cotton rates hold steady.</headline>
<dateline>KARACHI, Pakistan 1997-02-12</dateline>
<text>
<p>Pakistani cotton rates closed steady on Wednesday due to a lack of demand from well-stocked spinners, dealers said.</p>
<p>In the kerb market, the rate for NIAB-78 variety was quoted at 2,225 to 2,275 rupees per maund (37.32 kg), a dealer at the private Karachi Cotton Association (KCA) said.</p>
<p>He said the rate was likely to open stable on Thursday.  </p>
<p>Wednesday's KCA official spot rates in rupees per maund:</p>
<p>				     Wednesday	  Feb 11</p>
<p>    NIAB-78			2,322.50	   2,322.50</p>
<p>    K-68			   2,515		2,515</p>
<p>    MNH-93			 2,525		2,525</p>
<p>($1 = 40.22 rupees) -- Ibrahim Khan 9221-5685192</p>
